  "Pip Plans a Play\n\nOn the day of the puppet play, Pip needed a stage. A tray on the grass looked just right. Then one end tipped up when Pip touched the other. “My puppets will fall,” Pip said. Pip set the tray on a low, flat box. Now the puppets could stay on the tray for the play.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/bd4b08827bdc1086a8bb.mp3",
