  "Socks Threads the Beads\n\nOne bead after another slips onto Socks's long string. Then a bead stops at the tip. Clay fills its hole. Socks sets that bead aside and picks one with a clear hole. This one slips on. Socks ties the ends together and hangs the beads by the window.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/6d22b4df9d8b9c79e38d.mp3",
