  "Chips Keeps the Clay Soft\n\nThe clay animal on the tray still needed ears. There was no time left that day. Uncovered clay would be hard by morning. Chips laid a damp cloth over the animal and left it there. Next morning Chips shaped two ears from the still-soft clay.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/a2ec7c0d5a5142df3321.mp3",
