  "Fluff Sweeps the Doorway\n\nLeaves from a tree blow across the doorway. Fluff starts to sweep, but each gust blows more leaves in. Fluff sweeps the last leaves outside and pulls the door shut. Now the broom can go away. The shut door keeps new leaves from blowing in.": "/audio/production/en-US/comprehension/4ab3fb614600d112a034.mp3",
